.TH CTI-LOCK 1 "2026-11-22" "cti-agent 1.7" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-lock \- take a runner's lane lock on a file descriptor it holds open
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti\-lock
.BI \-\-fd " N"
.BI \-\-wait " SECONDS"
.BI \-\-who " TEXT"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti\-lock
is called by
.B fleet_lock
in
.IR share/fleet\-mode.sh ,
which every runner that changes something sources. It is not an operator
command.
.PP
The runner opens
.IR $FLEET_HOME/state/locks/ lane .lock
on descriptor 9 and keeps it open until it exits;
.B cti\-lock
takes flock(2) on that inherited descriptor. The lock belongs to the open
file, so the kernel releases it however the run ends (kill \-9 included)
and there is never a stale lock to clear. Once it holds the lock it
replaces the file's contents with
.IR TEXT ,
which another run prints when it finds the lane busy.
.PP
Another run's lock is retried every 5 seconds until
.I SECONDS
have passed; 0 refuses at once (a dry run never waits). What a runner does
then (a real run may go ahead beside a rehearsal, with a warning) is
.BR fleet_lock 's
decision, not this tool's.
.PP
It replaced a python3 snippet that was there only because macOS has no
flock(1). The runner looks for it beside
.I fleet\-mode.sh
in
.IR bin/ ,
then in
.IR $FLEET_CODE/bin ,
then on
.BR PATH ;
when it is missing the runner does not start.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-fd " N"
The descriptor to lock, 3 or more. The runners use 9.
.TP
.BI \-\-wait " SECONDS"
How long to wait for another run. Default 0.
.TP
.BI \-\-who " TEXT"
What to write in the lock file once it is held.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The lock is held.
.TP
.B 75
Another run still held it after
.I SECONDS
seconds.
.TP
.B 1
The descriptor could not be locked or written.
.TP
.B 2
Bad arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
See who holds the daily digest's lock, as a busy run reports it:
.PP
.EX
sudo cat /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/locks/digest\-daily.lock
.EE
.PP
What fleet_lock runs for a real run:
.PP
.EX
exec 9>>"$FLEET_HOME/state/locks/digest\-daily.lock"
cti\-lock \-\-fd 9 \-\-wait 600 \-\-who "pid $$, real run, started $(date '+%F %T')"
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/cti\-agent/bin/cti\-lock
The helper, root-owned.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/locks/
One lock file per lane, 0600.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-digest (1),
.BR run\-patchtuesday (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
